        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1e293b&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;How does an agent&amp;#39;s tool call reach a tool server, and who checks it on the way?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: the agentgateway MCP backend in front, ToolHive operator v1beta1 for third-party tool servers, the CMP&amp;#39;s own MCP server, proposal of 2026-10-25 · drawn in full: what the proposal adds (IA-2) · faded: what already runs&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: model calls (AI gateway internals) · OPA through extAuth per tool (IA-3) · ToolHive vMCP, not needed while the MCP backend serves all targets&lt;br&gt;Assumed: example tool server github-mcp-server over stdio; one mcp route and one AgentgatewayBackend mcp per gateway; tool tokens synced from Vault&lt;br&gt;v0.2 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp · docs.stacklok.com/toolhive · agentgateway docs (MCP connectivity, tool access)&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
