        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="keycloak__port_bottom_1590_894" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;TCP 80&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;html=1;fillColor=#e11d48;strokeColor=#f8fafc;strokeWidth=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=9;fontColor=#ffffff;movable=0;resizable=0;" vertex="1" parent="keycloak">
          <mxGeometry x="19.799999999999955" y="96" width="40.4" height="16" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n-th-two" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Two kinds of tool servers behind one /mcp: the CMP&amp;#39;s own MCP server, which already applies the stake policy per project, and third-party servers run by ToolHive, each in its own pod with its own token.&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4240" y="260" width="420" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n-th-names" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;The MCP backend lists the tools of all its targets behind one /mcp endpoint, so the agent sees one tool server. How names are kept apart across targets is for the phase 2 trial to confirm.&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4240" y="470" width="420" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n-th-stake" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Stake policy: allow runs at once, ask needs the user&amp;#39;s yes, PR opens a pull request, approve waits for an approver in the CMP, deny refuses. The agent never decides its own stake.&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="4240" y="660" width="420" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-steps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#059669&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Request path · an agent calls a tool&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; The agent sends tools/call to /mcp on the AI gateway with its JWT; jwtAuthentication and authorization check it as for a model call.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; The route match sends /mcp to the MCP proxy, which applies the AgentgatewayPolicy tools: CEL on the JWT claims and mcp.tool.name, allow only what matches.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; For a GitHub tool such as issue_read, the MCP proxy calls the ToolHive proxy of that server.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; The ToolHive proxy checks the JWT again (Keycloak issuer, audience), its Cedar policy and tool filter, then writes the JSON-RPC to the server&amp;#39;s stdin.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; github-mcp-server calls the GitHub API with its own token, never the agent&amp;#39;s.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt; For CMP tools, the MCP proxy calls the CMP&amp;#39;s MCP server, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; which evaluates the stake policy and calls the CMP API, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#0f172a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt; which commits or tags in the app repo.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2100" width="2250" height="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-background" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#d97706&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background · control plane and identity&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; The ToolHive operator watches MCPServer and writes the proxy Deployment, Service, ServiceAccount and Role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; The agentgateway controller watches the mcp route, the mcp backend and the tools policy, and configures the MCP proxy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; The ToolHive proxy creates the server pod and attaches to its stdio through the API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt; The ToolHive proxy and jwtAuthentication fetch Keycloak&amp;#39;s JWKS. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;F&lt;/span&gt; The agent gets its JWT from Keycloak. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; Code runs go to sandboxes (sandbox zoom).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2330" y="2100" width="2370" height="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-objects" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0284c7&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Objects · who points at whom&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• HTTPRoute mcp → AgentgatewayBackend mcp → Service mcp-github-proxy (and the CMP&amp;#39;s MCP service); AgentgatewayPolicy tools → the backend.&lt;br&gt;• MCPServer github → MCPToolConfig, MCPOIDCConfig, MCPTelemetryConfig, Secret github-token.&lt;br&gt;• Per MCPServer the operator generates a Deployment for the proxy, a Service and a ServiceAccount with its Role; the proxy creates the server pod.&lt;br&gt;• stdio servers run as one replica with one client: here the MCP proxy. Scale with streamable HTTP servers.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2410" width="2250" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-legend" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#64748b&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Legend&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2330" y="2410" width="2370" height="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
